<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Related works</h2>

<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">RL for diffusion and flow models.</span> RL for diffusion or flow models can be classified into two categories: <span id="A1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">a)</span> Only working with the reverse process, either by computing <em id="A1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">policy gradient</em> via accumulating the log probabilities over the diffusion timesteps <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib28" title="" class="ltx_ref">Black et al., 2023</a>; <a href="#bib.bib29" title="" class="ltx_ref">Fan et al., 2023</a>; <a href="#bib.bib54" title="" class="ltx_ref">Ren et al., 2024</a>; <a href="#bib.bib10" title="" class="ltx_ref">Liu et al., 2025</a>; <a href="#bib.bib11" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhang et al., 2025b</a>)</cite>, or directly backpropagating gradients through the reverse process by <em id="A1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">reparameterization</em> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib30" title="" class="ltx_ref">Clark et al., 2023</a>; <a href="#bib.bib52" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wang et al., 2024b</a>; <a href="#bib.bib31" title="" class="ltx_ref">Prabhudesai et al., 2024</a>; <a href="#bib.bib64" title="" class="ltx_ref">Celik et al., 2025</a>; <a href="#bib.bib33" title="" class="ltx_ref">Ding et al., 2025</a>; <a href="#bib.bib34" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhang et al., 2025c</a>; <a href="#bib.bib44" title="" class="ltx_ref">Gao et al., 2025</a>)</cite>. Such methods closely resemble standard RL algorithms, such as Proximal Policy Optimization (PPO) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib56" title="" class="ltx_ref">Schulman et al., 2017</a>)</cite> and Soft Actor Critic (SAC) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib48" title="" class="ltx_ref">Haarnoja et al., 2018</a>)</cite>, respectively. However, their computational cost typically scales linearly with the number of reverse diffusion steps <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib59" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wang et al., 2022</a>; <a href="#bib.bib44" title="" class="ltx_ref">Gao et al., 2025</a>)</cite>. Moreover, they require a training pipeline that is substantially different from standard score or flow matching, as we need to generate and differentiate through the denoising trajectory. <span id="A1.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">b)</span> Another way is preserving the forward process, and steering the score or flow prediction through <em id="A1.p1.1.6" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">weighted behavior cloning</em> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib50" title="" class="ltx_ref">Ding et al., 2024</a>; <a href="#bib.bib1" title="" class="ltx_ref">Ma et al., 2025a</a>; <a href="#bib.bib24" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhang et al., 2025a</a>; <a href="#bib.bib22" title="" class="ltx_ref">Tang et al., 2025</a>; <a href="#bib.bib32" title="" class="ltx_ref">Dong et al., 2025</a>)</cite> or <em id="A1.p1.1.7" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">moving towards calibrated targets</em> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib35" title="" class="ltx_ref">Lu et al., 2023</a>; <a href="#bib.bib47" title="" class="ltx_ref">Psenka et al., 2023</a>; <a href="#bib.bib8" title="" class="ltx_ref">Frans et al., 2025</a>; <a href="#bib.bib63" title="" class="ltx_ref">Akhound-Sadegh et al., 2024</a>)</cite>. In this way, the optimization is well-formulated as distribution matching. In this paper, we dive into the weighted flow matching formula and explore more reweighting options.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Regularizations in policy extraction.</span> KL divergence is widely adopted to regularize the policy regularization and improvement <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib65" title="" class="ltx_ref">Peng et al., 2019</a>; <a href="#bib.bib23" title="" class="ltx_ref">Vieillard et al., 2020</a>; <a href="#bib.bib36" title="" class="ltx_ref">Nair et al., 2020</a>)</cite>. However, it is also possible to adopt other types of divergence metrics. Several works also consider reverse KL regularization <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib17" title="" class="ltx_ref">Xu et al., 2025</a>; <a href="#bib.bib18" title="" class="ltx_ref">Ma et al., 2025b</a>)</cite>, leading to update rules similar to policy gradient theorems. <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib15" title="" class="ltx_ref">Xu et al. (2023)</a>; <a href="#bib.bib17" title="" class="ltx_ref">Xu et al. (2025)</a></cite> further study implicit value regularization, which derives closed-form target policies and update rules for general <math id="A1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math>-divergence regularized problems. In this paper, we deepen this understanding by extending it to signed measures, thus allowing more flexible and effective objective design. Finally, another branch of research about policy mirror descent is motivated by the Bregman divergence <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib60" title="" class="ltx_ref">Tomar et al., 2021</a>; <a href="#bib.bib19" title="" class="ltx_ref">Shani et al., 2020</a>)</cite>. Notably, the KL divergence occupies a special position, as it is both a Bregman divergence and an <math id="A1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math>-divergence.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Leveraging negative samples in RL for diffusion models.</span> Negative weights are typically underutilized in weighted behavior cloning and best-of-N distillation. To better exploit such samples in diffusion models, <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib8" title="" class="ltx_ref">Frans et al. (2025)</a>; <a href="#bib.bib9" title="" class="ltx_ref">Physical Intelligence et al. (2025)</a>; <a href="#bib.bib16" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zheng et al. (2025)</a></cite> used reward or advantage functions to classify data into preference pairs, and reinforced the diffusion model with classifier-free guidance. <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib22" title="" class="ltx_ref">Tang et al. (2025)</a></cite> leveraged a weighted behavior cloning with negative weights for diffusion language model reasoning. However, the negative reweighting function is an ad-hoc design, while we provide a generalized and unified viewpoint with theoretical justification.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span><math id="A2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math>-divergence on Signed measure.</h2>

<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q</annotation></semantics></math> be a finite nonnegative measure (e.g., a probability measure) and let <math id="A2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math> be a finite signed measure. Assume the total variation of <math id="A2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math> is absolutely continuous with respect to <math id="A2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q</annotation></semantics></math>, i.e., <math id="A2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|P|\ll Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≪</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|P|\ll Q</annotation></semantics></math>, so that the Radon–Nikodym derivative <math id="A2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r:=dP/dQ" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r:=dP/dQ</annotation></semantics></math> exists <math id="A2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q</annotation></semantics></math>-a.e. and may take negative values. If <math id="A2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> is extended to a measurable function on <math id="A2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ℝ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math> (or at least on the essential range of <math id="A2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math>) such that <math id="A2.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(r)\in L^{1}(Q)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(r)\in L^{1}(Q)</annotation></semantics></math>, we define</p>
<table id="A2.Ex10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="D_{f}(P\|Q)\;:=\;\int f\!\left(\frac{dP}{dQ}\right)\,dQ." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo rspace="0.280em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.391em">:=</mo><mo>∫</mo><mpadded style="width:0.427em;" width="0.427em"><mi>f</mi></mpadded><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo rspace="0.170em">)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{f}(P\|Q)\;:=\;\int f\!\left(\frac{dP}{dQ}\right)\,dQ.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Moreover, if <math id="A2.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q</annotation></semantics></math> is a probability measure, <math id="A2.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P(\Omega)=Q(\Omega)=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P(\Omega)=Q(\Omega)=1</annotation></semantics></math>, and the extension of <math id="A2.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> is convex on <math id="A2.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ℝ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A2.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(1)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(1)=0</annotation></semantics></math>, then Jensen’s inequality yields <math id="A2.p1.m17" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="D_{f}(P\|Q)\geqslant 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⩾</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{f}(P\|Q)\geqslant 0</annotation></semantics></math> despite <math id="A2.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math> potentially being negative; under strict convexity, the usual identity-of-indiscernibles conclusion <math id="A2.p1.m19" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="D_{f}(P\|Q)=0\Rightarrow P=Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">⇒</mo><mi>P</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{f}(P\|Q)=0\Rightarrow P=Q</annotation></semantics></math> follows (up to standard regularity/equality conditions).</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Derivations</h2>

<section id="A3.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.1 </span>Derivation of the <math id="A3.SS1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math>-Divergence Regularized Policy Optimization</h3>

<div id="A3.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">We omit the state <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝒔</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{s}</annotation></semantics></math> in the following derivation for brevity. Let <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f:\mathbb{R}^{+}\to\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f:\mathbb{R}^{+}\to\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math> be strictly convex and differentiable and <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(1)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(1)=0</annotation></semantics></math>. We want to find a policy <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi\in\Pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi\in\Pi</annotation></semantics></math> that maximizes the value <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q(\bm{a})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q(\bm{a})</annotation></semantics></math> while controlling the <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math>-divergence from the behavior policy <math id="A3.SS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\rm old}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>old</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\rm old}</annotation></semantics></math>, which can be formulated as the following constrained optimization problem:</p>
<table id="A3.E12" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A3.E12X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E12X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\max_{\pi\in\Pi}\ \sum_{\bm{a}\in\mathcal{A}}\pi(\bm{a})Q(\bm{a})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mmultiscripts><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>𝒂</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow></munder><mprescripts></mprescripts><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi></mrow><mrow></mrow></mmultiscripts></mstyle><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\max_{\pi\in\Pi}\ \sum_{\bm{a}\in\mathcal{A}}\pi(\bm{a})Q(\bm{a})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="2" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(12)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A3.E12Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E12Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\text{s.t.}\left\{\begin{aligned} D_{f}(\pi(\cdot)\|\pi_{\rm old}(\cdot))&amp;\leqslant\epsilon\\
\sum_{\bm{a}\in\mathcal{A}}\pi(\bm{a})&amp;=1\\
\forall\bm{a}\in\mathcal{A},\ \ \pi(\bm{a})&amp;\geqslant 0\end{aligned}\right." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>s.t.</mtext><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="0pt" rowspacing="1.0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mi>D</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>f</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>old</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⩽</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>𝒂</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>𝒂</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⩾</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\text{s.t.}\left\{\begin{aligned} D_{f}(\pi(\cdot)\|\pi_{\rm old}(\cdot))&amp;\leqslant\epsilon\\
\sum_{\bm{a}\in\mathcal{A}}\pi(\bm{a})&amp;=1\\
\forall\bm{a}\in\mathcal{A},\ \ \pi(\bm{a})&amp;\geqslant 0\end{aligned}\right.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">We introduce Lagrange multipliers <math id="A3.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A3.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ν</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A3.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta(\bm{a})\geqslant 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⩾</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta(\bm{a})\geqslant 0</annotation></semantics></math> for the constraints, respectively, leading to the following Lagrange function <math id="A3.SS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A3.E13" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A3.E13X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E13X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{L}(\pi,\lambda,\nu,\eta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ν</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>η</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{L}(\pi,\lambda,\nu,\eta)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E13X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{\bm{a}\in\mathcal{A}}\pi(\bm{a})Q(\bm{a})-\lambda\left(\sum_{\bm{a}\in\mathcal{A}}\pi_{\rm old}(\bm{a})f\left(\frac{\pi(\bm{a})}{\pi_{\rm old}(\bm{a})}\right)-\epsilon\right)-\nu(1-\sum_{\bm{a}\in\mathcal{A}}\pi(\bm{a}))+\sum_{\bm{a}\in\mathcal{A}}\eta(\bm{a})\pi(\bm{a})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>𝒂</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>𝒂</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>old</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>old</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>𝒂</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>𝒂</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{\bm{a}\in\mathcal{A}}\pi(\bm{a})Q(\bm{a})-\lambda\left(\sum_{\bm{a}\in\mathcal{A}}\pi_{\rm old}(\bm{a})f\left(\frac{\pi(\bm{a})}{\pi_{\rm old}(\bm{a})}\right)-\epsilon\right)-\nu(1-\sum_{\bm{a}\in\mathcal{A}}\pi(\bm{a}))+\sum_{\bm{a}\in\mathcal{A}}\eta(\bm{a})\pi(\bm{a}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(13)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.p2.3" class="ltx_p">We take the functional derivative with respect to <math id="A3.SS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi(\bm{a})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi(\bm{a})</annotation></semantics></math> and set it to zero. Recall that the derivative of the term <math id="A3.SS1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu f(\pi/\mu)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu f(\pi/\mu)</annotation></semantics></math> with respect to <math id="A3.SS1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A3.SS1.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f^{\prime}(\pi/\mu)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f^{\prime}(\pi/\mu)</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A3.E14" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A3.E14X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E14X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle 0=\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial\pi(\bm{a})}=Q(\bm{a})-\lambda f^{\prime}(\frac{\pi(\bm{a})}{\pi_{\rm old}(\bm{a})})-\nu+\eta(\bm{a})," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>old</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>ν</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle 0=\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial\pi(\bm{a})}=Q(\bm{a})-\lambda f^{\prime}(\frac{\pi(\bm{a})}{\pi_{\rm old}(\bm{a})})-\nu+\eta(\bm{a}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(14)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.p2.4" class="ltx_p">Rearranging to isolate the divergence term,</p>
<table id="A3.E15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f^{\prime}\left(\frac{\pi(\bm{a})}{\pi_{\rm old}(\bm{a})}\right)=\frac{Q(\bm{a})-\nu+\eta(\bm{a})}{\lambda}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>old</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>ν</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mi>λ</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f^{\prime}\left(\frac{\pi(\bm{a})}{\pi_{\rm old}(\bm{a})}\right)=\frac{Q(\bm{a})-\nu+\eta(\bm{a})}{\lambda}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(15)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.p3.2" class="ltx_p">We define <math id="A3.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{f}=(f^{\prime})^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{f}=(f^{\prime})^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math>. Since the complimentary slackness requires <math id="A3.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta(\bm{a})\pi(\bm{a})=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta(\bm{a})\pi(\bm{a})=0</annotation></semantics></math>, we consider the following cases:</p>
<ul id="A3.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A3.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A3.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi(\bm{a})&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi(\bm{a})&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, in this case <math id="A3.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta(\bm{a})=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta(\bm{a})=0</annotation></semantics></math>, therefore we have</p>
<table id="A3.Ex11" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex11X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex11X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle f^{\prime}\left(\frac{\pi(\bm{a})}{\pi_{\rm old}(\bm{a})}\right)=\frac{Q(\bm{a})-\nu}{\lambda}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>old</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>ν</mi></mrow><mi>λ</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle f^{\prime}\left(\frac{\pi(\bm{a})}{\pi_{\rm old}(\bm{a})}\right)=\frac{Q(\bm{a})-\nu}{\lambda}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex11X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Rightarrow\frac{\pi(\bm{a})}{\pi_{\rm old}(\bm{a})}=g_{f}\left(\frac{Q(\bm{a})-\nu}{\lambda}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo stretchy="false">⇒</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>old</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>ν</mi></mrow><mi>λ</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Rightarrow\frac{\pi(\bm{a})}{\pi_{\rm old}(\bm{a})}=g_{f}\left(\frac{Q(\bm{a})-\nu}{\lambda}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.I1.i1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Besides, since <math id="A3.I1.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> is strongly convex, both <math id="A3.I1.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.I1.i1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{f}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{f}</annotation></semantics></math> are increasing, therefore</p>
<table id="A3.Ex12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{Q(\bm{a})-\nu}{\lambda}=f^{\prime}(\frac{\pi(\bm{a})}{\pi_{\rm old}(\bm{a})})&gt;f^{\prime}(0)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>ν</mi></mrow><mi>λ</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>old</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{Q(\bm{a})-\nu}{\lambda}=f^{\prime}(\frac{\pi(\bm{a})}{\pi_{\rm old}(\bm{a})})&gt;f^{\prime}(0).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A3.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi(\bm{a})=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi(\bm{a})=0</annotation></semantics></math>, in this case <math id="A3.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta(\bm{a})&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta(\bm{a})&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>. From the stationary condition, we know that</p>
<table id="A3.Ex13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q(\bm{a})-\nu+\eta(\bm{a})=\lambda f^{\prime}(0)\Rightarrow\frac{Q(\bm{a})-\nu}{\lambda}&lt;f^{\prime}(0)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>ν</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⇒</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>ν</mi></mrow><mi>λ</mi></mfrac><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q(\bm{a})-\nu+\eta(\bm{a})=\lambda f^{\prime}(0)\Rightarrow\frac{Q(\bm{a})-\nu}{\lambda}&lt;f^{\prime}(0).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
</ul>
<p id="A3.SS1.p3.3" class="ltx_p">Therefore, for both cases, we can unify the optimal solution as</p>
<table id="A3.E16" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A3.E16X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E16X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\pi(\bm{a})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\pi(\bm{a})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E16X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\pi_{\rm old}(\bm{a})\bar{g}_{f}\left(\frac{Q(\bm{a})-\nu}{\lambda}\right)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>old</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>f</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>ν</mi></mrow><mi>λ</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\pi_{\rm old}(\bm{a})\bar{g}_{f}\left(\frac{Q(\bm{a})-\nu}{\lambda}\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(16)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.p3.4" class="ltx_p">where</p>
<table id="A3.E17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E17.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\bar{g}_{f}(x)=\left\{\begin{aligned} &amp;g_{f}(x)\quad&amp;\text{if }x&gt;f^{\prime}(0)\\
&amp;0&amp;\text{if }x\leqslant f^{\prime}(0)\end{aligned}\right.." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>f</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="0pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="1.0pt"><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{g}_{f}(x)=\left\{\begin{aligned} &amp;g_{f}(x)\quad&amp;\text{if }x&gt;f^{\prime}(0)\\
&amp;0&amp;\text{if }x\leqslant f^{\prime}(0)\end{aligned}\right..</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(17)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.2 </span>Derivation of the <math id="A3.SS2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math>-Divergence Regularized Policy Optimization on Signed Measures</h3>

<div id="A3.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(x):\mathbb{R}\to\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>ℝ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(x):\mathbb{R}\to\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math> be strictly convex and differentiable and <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(1)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(1)=0</annotation></semantics></math>. Since <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> is strictly convex, <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> is monotonically increasing, and therefore <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{f}=(f^{\prime})^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{f}=(f^{\prime})^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math> is well defined. Consider the solution space <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{\Pi}=\{\pi:\sum_{\bm{a}\sim\mathcal{A}}\pi(\bm{a})=1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.111em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>𝒂</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{\Pi}=\{\pi:\sum_{\bm{a}\sim\mathcal{A}}\pi(\bm{a})=1\}</annotation></semantics></math>, the optimization problem regularized the generalized <math id="A3.SS2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math>-divergence is defined as</p>
<table id="A3.E18" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A3.E18X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E18X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\max_{\pi\in\widetilde{\Pi}}\ \sum_{\bm{a}\in\mathcal{A}}\pi(\bm{a})Q(\bm{a})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mmultiscripts><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>𝒂</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow></munder><mprescripts></mprescripts><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>∈</mo><mover accent="true"><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mrow></mrow></mmultiscripts></mstyle><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\max_{\pi\in\widetilde{\Pi}}\ \sum_{\bm{a}\in\mathcal{A}}\pi(\bm{a})Q(\bm{a})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="2" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(18)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A3.E18Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E18Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\text{s.t.}\left\{\begin{aligned} D_{{f}}(\pi(\cdot)\|\pi_{\rm old}(\cdot))&amp;\leqslant\epsilon\\
\sum_{\bm{a}\in\mathcal{A}}\pi(\bm{a})&amp;=1\\
\end{aligned}\right." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>s.t.</mtext><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="0pt" rowspacing="1.0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mi>D</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>f</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>old</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⩽</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>𝒂</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\text{s.t.}\left\{\begin{aligned} D_{{f}}(\pi(\cdot)\|\pi_{\rm old}(\cdot))&amp;\leqslant\epsilon\\
\sum_{\bm{a}\in\mathcal{A}}\pi(\bm{a})&amp;=1\\
\end{aligned}\right.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We introduce Lagrange multipliers <math id="A3.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ν</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu</annotation></semantics></math> for the constraints, leading to the following Lagrange function <math id="A3.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A3.E19" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A3.E19X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E19X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{L}(\pi,\lambda,\nu)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ν</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{L}(\pi,\lambda,\nu)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E19X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{\bm{a}\in\mathcal{A}}\pi(\bm{a})Q(\bm{a})-\lambda\left(\sum_{\bm{a}\in\mathcal{A}}\pi_{\rm old}(\bm{a})f\left(\frac{\pi(\bm{a})}{\pi_{\rm old}(\bm{a})}\right)-\epsilon\right)-\nu(1-\sum_{\bm{a}\in\mathcal{A}}\pi(\bm{a}))." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>𝒂</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>𝒂</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>old</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>old</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>ν</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>𝒂</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{\bm{a}\in\mathcal{A}}\pi(\bm{a})Q(\bm{a})-\lambda\left(\sum_{\bm{a}\in\mathcal{A}}\pi_{\rm old}(\bm{a})f\left(\frac{\pi(\bm{a})}{\pi_{\rm old}(\bm{a})}\right)-\epsilon\right)-\nu(1-\sum_{\bm{a}\in\mathcal{A}}\pi(\bm{a})).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(19)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p2.2" class="ltx_p">Taking its derivative w.r.t. <math id="A3.SS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi(\bm{a})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi(\bm{a})</annotation></semantics></math> and setting it to zero:</p>
<table id="A3.E20" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A3.E20X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E20X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle 0=\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial\pi(\bm{a})}=Q(\bm{a})-\lambda f^{\prime}\left(\frac{\pi(\bm{a})}{\pi_{\rm old}(\bm{a})}\right)-\nu," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>old</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>ν</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle 0=\frac{\partial\mathcal{L}}{\partial\pi(\bm{a})}=Q(\bm{a})-\lambda f^{\prime}\left(\frac{\pi(\bm{a})}{\pi_{\rm old}(\bm{a})}\right)-\nu,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(20)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p2.3" class="ltx_p">i.e.,</p>
<table id="A3.Ex14" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex14X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex14X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\pi(\bm{a})=\pi_{\rm old}(\bm{a})(f^{\prime})^{-1}\left(\frac{Q(\bm{a})-\nu}{\lambda}\right)=\pi_{\rm old}(\bm{a})g_{f}\left(\frac{Q(\bm{a})-\nu}{\lambda}\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>old</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>ν</mi></mrow><mi>λ</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>old</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>ν</mi></mrow><mi>λ</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\pi(\bm{a})=\pi_{\rm old}(\bm{a})(f^{\prime})^{-1}\left(\frac{Q(\bm{a})-\nu}{\lambda}\right)=\pi_{\rm old}(\bm{a})g_{f}\left(\frac{Q(\bm{a})-\nu}{\lambda}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p2.4" class="ltx_p">Note that <math id="A3.SS2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ν</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu</annotation></semantics></math> is the normalization term such that <math id="A3.SS2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{\bm{a}\in\mathcal{A}}\mu(\bm{a})g\left((Q(\bm{a})-\nu)/\lambda\right)=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>𝒂</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>ν</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{\bm{a}\in\mathcal{A}}\mu(\bm{a})g\left((Q(\bm{a})-\nu)/\lambda\right)=1</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Generally speaking, for any strictly increasing (and typically continuous) function <math id="A3.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g</annotation></semantics></math> defined on an interval <math id="A3.SS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I\subseteq\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I\subseteq\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math>, its inverse <math id="A3.SS2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math> exists on <math id="A3.SS2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g(I)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g(I)</annotation></semantics></math> and is strictly increasing. Define <math id="A3.SS2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f^{\prime}_{g}(x)=g^{-1}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mi>g</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f^{\prime}_{g}(x)=g^{-1}(x)</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A3.SS2.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in g(I)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in g(I)</annotation></semantics></math> and</p>
<table id="A3.Ex15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{g}(x)=\int_{\bm{a}_{0}}^{x}g^{-1}(t)\mathrm{d}t+C" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mi>x</mi></msubsup><mrow><msup><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{g}(x)=\int_{\bm{a}_{0}}^{x}g^{-1}(t)\mathrm{d}t+C</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p3.2" class="ltx_p">yields a differentiable strictly convex function on <math id="A3.SS2.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g(I)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g(I)</annotation></semantics></math>. Normalizing <math id="A3.SS2.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{g}(1)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{g}(1)=0</annotation></semantics></math> underpins <math id="A3.SS2.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math>. While the analytic formulation of <math id="A3.SS2.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{g}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{g}</annotation></semantics></math> may not be available for an arbitrary <math id="A3.SS2.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g</annotation></semantics></math>, this observation allows us to reason directly in terms of the weighting function <math id="A3.SS2.p3.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g</annotation></semantics></math> rather than <math id="A3.SS2.p3.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{g}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>g</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{g}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.3 </span>Policy Improvement Property of the Target Measure</h3>

<div id="A3.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem C.1</span></span><span id="A3.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Theorem <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem5" title="Theorem 3.5 (Guaranteed policy improvement, proof in Appendix ). ‣ 3.3 Negative Reweighting by Extending 𝑓-divergence Definition to Signed Measures ‣ 3 A Unified Framework for Reweighting with Measure Matching ‣ SiMPO: Measure Matching for Online Diffusion Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.5</span></a> restated)<span id="A3.Thmtheorem1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Assume <math id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g:\mathbb{R}\to\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>ℝ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g:\mathbb{R}\to\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math> is monotonic increasing and the target measure <math id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\pi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\pi}</annotation></semantics></math> is defined as</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\pi}(\bm{a}|\bm{s})=\pi(\bm{a}|\bm{s})g\left(\frac{Q(\bm{s},\bm{a})-\nu}{\lambda}\right)\quad\forall\bm{s}\in{\mathcal{S}}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>ν</mi></mrow><mi>λ</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1.167em;" width="1.167em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>𝒔</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\pi}(\bm{a}|\bm{s})=\pi(\bm{a}|\bm{s})g\left(\frac{Q(\bm{s},\bm{a})-\nu}{\lambda}\right)\quad\forall\bm{s}\in{\mathcal{S}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ν</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nu</annotation></semantics></math> is selected such that <math id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{\bm{a}\in\mathcal{A}}\tilde{\pi}(\bm{a}|\bm{s})=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>𝐚</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐚</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝐬</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{\bm{a}\in\mathcal{A}}\tilde{\pi}(\bm{a}|\bm{s})=1</annotation></semantics></math> holds. Then we have</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{\bm{a}\in\mathcal{A}}\tilde{\pi}(\bm{a}|\bm{s})Q(\bm{s},\bm{a})\geqslant\sum_{\bm{a}\in\mathcal{A}}\pi(\bm{a}|\bm{s})Q(\bm{s},\bm{a})\quad\forall\bm{s}\in{\mathcal{S}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>𝒂</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">⩾</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>𝒂</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1.167em;" width="1.167em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>𝒔</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{\bm{a}\in\mathcal{A}}\tilde{\pi}(\bm{a}|\bm{s})Q(\bm{s},\bm{a})\geqslant\sum_{\bm{a}\in\mathcal{A}}\pi(\bm{a}|\bm{s})Q(\bm{s},\bm{a})\quad\forall\bm{s}\in{\mathcal{S}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A3.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">Denote <math id="A3.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A(\bm{s},\bm{a})=\frac{Q(\bm{s},\bm{a})-\nu}{\lambda}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>ν</mi></mrow><mi>λ</mi></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A(\bm{s},\bm{a})=\frac{Q(\bm{s},\bm{a})-\nu}{\lambda}</annotation></semantics></math>, and thus we have <math id="A3.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\sum_{\bm{a}\in\mathcal{A}}\tilde{\pi}(\bm{a}|\bm{s})=\mathbb{E}_{\pi}[g\left(A(\bm{s},\bm{a})\right]=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>𝒂</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow></msub><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>π</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{\bm{a}\in\mathcal{A}}\tilde{\pi}(\bm{a}|\bm{s})=\mathbb{E}_{\pi}[g\left(A(\bm{s},\bm{a})\right]=1</annotation></semantics></math>. It suffices to show</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{\bm{a}\in\mathcal{A}}\tilde{\pi}(\bm{a}|\bm{s})A(\bm{s},\bm{a})\geqslant\sum_{\bm{a}\in\mathcal{A}}\pi(\bm{a}|\bm{s})A(\bm{s},\bm{a})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>𝒂</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">⩾</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>𝒂</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{\bm{a}\in\mathcal{A}}\tilde{\pi}(\bm{a}|\bm{s})A(\bm{s},\bm{a})\geqslant\sum_{\bm{a}\in\mathcal{A}}\pi(\bm{a}|\bm{s})A(\bm{s},\bm{a}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text">Consider the difference</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex19" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex19X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex19X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{\bm{a}\in\mathcal{A}}\tilde{\pi}(\bm{a}|\bm{s})A(\bm{s},\bm{a})-\sum_{\bm{a}\in\mathcal{A}}\pi(\bm{a}|\bm{s})A(\bm{s},\bm{a})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>𝒂</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>𝒂</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{\bm{a}\in\mathcal{A}}\tilde{\pi}(\bm{a}|\bm{s})A(\bm{s},\bm{a})-\sum_{\bm{a}\in\mathcal{A}}\pi(\bm{a}|\bm{s})A(\bm{s},\bm{a})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex19Xa"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex19Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{\bm{a}\in\mathcal{A}}\pi(\bm{a}|\bm{s})A(\bm{s},\bm{a})g\left(A(\bm{s},\bm{a})\right)-\left(\sum_{\bm{a}\in\mathcal{A}}\pi(\bm{a}|\bm{s})A(\bm{s},\bm{a})\right)\left(\sum_{\bm{a}\in\mathcal{A}}\pi(\bm{a}|\bm{s})g\left(A(\bm{s},\bm{a})\right)\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>𝒂</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>𝒂</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>𝒂</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{\bm{a}\in\mathcal{A}}\pi(\bm{a}|\bm{s})A(\bm{s},\bm{a})g\left(A(\bm{s},\bm{a})\right)-\left(\sum_{\bm{a}\in\mathcal{A}}\pi(\bm{a}|\bm{s})A(\bm{s},\bm{a})\right)\left(\sum_{\bm{a}\in\mathcal{A}}\pi(\bm{a}|\bm{s})g\left(A(\bm{s},\bm{a})\right)\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex19Xb"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex19Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{\pi}[A(\bm{s},\bm{a})g\left(A(\bm{s},\bm{a})\right)]-\mathbb{E}_{\pi}[A(\bm{s},\bm{a})]\mathbb{E}_{\pi}[g\left(A(\bm{s},\bm{a})\right)]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>π</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>π</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>π</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{\pi}[A(\bm{s},\bm{a})g\left(A(\bm{s},\bm{a})\right)]-\mathbb{E}_{\pi}[A(\bm{s},\bm{a})]\mathbb{E}_{\pi}[g\left(A(\bm{s},\bm{a})\right)]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex19Xc"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex19Xc.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\text{Cov}_{\pi}[A(\bm{s},\bm{a}),g\left(A(\bm{s},\bm{a})\right)]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mtext>Cov</mtext><mi>π</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\text{Cov}_{\pi}[A(\bm{s},\bm{a}),g\left(A(\bm{s},\bm{a})\right)].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="A3.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g</annotation></semantics></math> is monotonic increasing, we know that <math id="A3.SS3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{Cov}_{\pi}[A(\bm{s},\bm{a}),g\left(A(\bm{s},\bm{a})\right)]\geqslant 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mtext>Cov</mtext><mi>π</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⩾</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{Cov}_{\pi}[A(\bm{s},\bm{a}),g\left(A(\bm{s},\bm{a})\right)]\geqslant 0</annotation></semantics></math>, and thus</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex20" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{\bm{a}\in\mathcal{A}}\tilde{\pi}(\bm{a}|\bm{s})A(\bm{s},\bm{a})\geqslant\sum_{\bm{a}\in\mathcal{A}}\pi(\bm{a}|\bm{s})A(\bm{s},\bm{a})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>𝒂</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">⩾</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>𝒂</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{\bm{a}\in\mathcal{A}}\tilde{\pi}(\bm{a}|\bm{s})A(\bm{s},\bm{a})\geqslant\sum_{\bm{a}\in\mathcal{A}}\pi(\bm{a}|\bm{s})A(\bm{s},\bm{a}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p1.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p1.4.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A4" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix D </span>Derivation of Closed-Form Solution of Reweighted Conditional Flow Matching.</h2>

<div id="A4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Notation. </span>We temporarily omit conditioning on the state <math id="A4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝒔</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{s}</annotation></semantics></math> for clarity.</p>
</div>
<section id="A4.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.1 </span>Closed-Form Solution of Conditional Flow Matching.</h3>

<div id="A4.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To warm up, we first show the optimal solution of flow matching when there is no reweighting factor <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w(\bm{a})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w(\bm{a})</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma D.1</span></span><span id="A4.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Conditional flow matching fits marginal velocity <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib6" title="" class="ltx_ref">Lipman et al., 2022</a>)</cite>.)<span id="A4.Thmtheorem1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The Conditional Flow Matching loss function is defined as:</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex21" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex21.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{\rm CFM}(\theta)=\mathbb{E}_{t\sim\mathcal{U}[0,1],\ \bm{a}_{0}\sim\pi_{\rm old}(\bm{a}_{0}),\ \bm{a}_{t}\sim p_{t}(\cdot|\bm{a}_{0})}\left[\|D_{\theta}(\bm{a}_{t};t)-\bm{v}_{t}(\bm{a}_{t}|\bm{a}_{0})\|^{2}\right]" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>CFM</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo><mo rspace="0.577em">,</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∼</mo><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>old</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo rspace="0.577em">,</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>;</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝒗</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{\rm CFM}(\theta)=\mathbb{E}_{t\sim\mathcal{U}[0,1],\ \bm{a}_{0}\sim\pi_{\rm old}(\bm{a}_{0}),\ \bm{a}_{t}\sim p_{t}(\cdot|\bm{a}_{0})}\left[\|D_{\theta}(\bm{a}_{t};t)-\bm{v}_{t}(\bm{a}_{t}|\bm{a}_{0})\|^{2}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A4.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">To find the minimum, we look for the vector field <math id="A4.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v(x)</annotation></semantics></math> that minimizes the objective at any specific point in space and time.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Step 1: Rewrite the Expectation.<span id="A4.SS1.p3.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">
We expand the expectation integrals over the joint distribution of data <math id="A4.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{a}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{a}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> and intermediate samples <math id="A4.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex22" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}=\int_{0}^{1}\int\int\pi_{\rm old}(\bm{a}_{0})p_{t|0}(\bm{a}|\bm{a}_{0})\|D_{\theta}(\bm{a}_{t};t)-\bm{v}_{t}(\bm{a}_{t}|\bm{a}_{0})\|^{2}\,d\bm{a}_{0}\,d\bm{a}_{t}\,dt" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><mo>∫</mo></mrow><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>old</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒗</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}=\int_{0}^{1}\int\int\pi_{\rm old}(\bm{a}_{0})p_{t|0}(\bm{a}|\bm{a}_{0})\|D_{\theta}(\bm{a}_{t};t)-\bm{v}_{t}(\bm{a}_{t}|\bm{a}_{0})\|^{2}\,d\bm{a}_{0}\,d\bm{a}_{t}\,dt</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS1.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Step 2: Apply Bayes’ Rule.<span id="A4.SS1.p3.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">
We can decompose the joint distribution <math id="A4.SS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\rm old}(\bm{a}_{0})p_{t|0}(\bm{a}|\bm{a}_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>old</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\rm old}(\bm{a}_{0})p_{t|0}(\bm{a}|\bm{a}_{0})</annotation></semantics></math> in the reverse direction using the marginal <math id="A4.SS1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{t}(\bm{a}_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{t}(\bm{a}_{t})</annotation></semantics></math> and the posterior <math id="A4.SS1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{0|t}(\bm{a}_{0}|\bm{a}_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{0|t}(\bm{a}_{0}|\bm{a}_{t})</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex23" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\rm old}(\bm{a}_{0})p_{t|0}(\bm{a}_{t}|\bm{a}_{0})=p_{t}(\bm{a}_{t})p_{0|t}(\bm{a}_{0}|\bm{a}_{t})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>old</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\rm old}(\bm{a}_{0})p_{t|0}(\bm{a}_{t}|\bm{a}_{0})=p_{t}(\bm{a}_{t})p_{0|t}(\bm{a}_{0}|\bm{a}_{t})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS1.p3.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.p3.3.1" class="ltx_text">Substitute this into the loss integral:</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex24" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}=\int_{0}^{1}\int p_{t}(\bm{a}_{t})\left[\int p_{0|t}(\bm{a}_{0}|\bm{a}_{t})\|D_{\theta}(\bm{a}_{t};t)-\bm{v}_{t}(\bm{a}_{t}|\bm{a}_{0})\|^{2}\,d\bm{a}_{0}\right]\,d\bm{a}_{t}\,dt" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em">∫</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒗</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}=\int_{0}^{1}\int p_{t}(\bm{a}_{t})\left[\int p_{0|t}(\bm{a}_{0}|\bm{a}_{t})\|D_{\theta}(\bm{a}_{t};t)-\bm{v}_{t}(\bm{a}_{t}|\bm{a}_{0})\|^{2}\,d\bm{a}_{0}\right]\,d\bm{a}_{t}\,dt</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS1.p3.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.p3.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Step 3: Pointwise Minimization.<span id="A4.SS1.p3.4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">
Since <math id="A4.SS1.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{t}(\bm{a}_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{t}(\bm{a}_{t})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.SS1.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="dt" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">dt</annotation></semantics></math> are non-negative, minimizing the total integral is equivalent to minimizing the inner term (the term in square brackets) for every specific location <math id="A4.SS1.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{a}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{a}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> and time <math id="A4.SS1.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>. Define the local objective <math id="A4.SS1.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J(v)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J(v)</annotation></semantics></math> for a fixed <math id="A4.SS1.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{a}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{a}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.SS1.p3.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex25" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J(v)=\int p_{0|t}(\bm{a}_{0}|\bm{a}_{t})\|v-\bm{v}_{t}(\bm{a}_{t}|\bm{a}_{0})\|^{2}\,d\bm{a}_{0}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒗</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J(v)=\int p_{0|t}(\bm{a}_{0}|\bm{a}_{t})\|v-\bm{v}_{t}(\bm{a}_{t}|\bm{a}_{0})\|^{2}\,d\bm{a}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS1.p3.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.p3.5.1" class="ltx_text">This is a standard Least Squares problem. We are looking for a constant vector <math id="A4.SS1.p3.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> (constant with respect to <math id="A4.SS1.p3.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{a}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{a}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>) that minimizes the expected squared distance to the random variable <math id="A4.SS1.p3.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{v}_{t}(\bm{a}_{t}|\bm{a}_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝒗</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{v}_{t}(\bm{a}_{t}|\bm{a}_{0})</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Step 4: Solve for <math id="A4.SS1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math>.<span id="A4.SS1.p4.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">
We take the gradient of <math id="A4.SS1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J(v)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J(v)</annotation></semantics></math> with respect to <math id="A4.SS1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> and set it to zero:</span></span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex26" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{v}J(v)=\int p_{0|t}(\bm{a}_{0}|\bm{a}_{t})\cdot 2(v-\bm{v}_{t}(\bm{a}_{t}|\bm{a}_{0}))\,d\bm{a}_{0}=0" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>v</mi></msub><mi>J</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒗</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{v}J(v)=\int p_{0|t}(\bm{a}_{0}|\bm{a}_{t})\cdot 2(v-\bm{v}_{t}(\bm{a}_{t}|\bm{a}_{0}))\,d\bm{a}_{0}=0</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="A4.Ex27" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\int p_{0|t}(\bm{a}_{0}|\bm{a}_{t})v\,d\bm{a}_{0}=\int p_{0|t}(\bm{a}_{0}|\bm{a}_{t})\bm{v}_{t}(\bm{a}_{t}|\bm{a}_{0})\,d\bm{a}_{0}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒗</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int p_{0|t}(\bm{a}_{0}|\bm{a}_{t})v\,d\bm{a}_{0}=\int p_{0|t}(\bm{a}_{0}|\bm{a}_{t})\bm{v}_{t}(\bm{a}_{t}|\bm{a}_{0})\,d\bm{a}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS1.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="A4.SS1.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> does not depend on <math id="A4.SS1.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{a}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{a}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>, we pull it out of the integral. Note that <math id="A4.SS1.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\int p_{0|t}(\bm{a}_{0}|\bm{a}_{t})d\bm{a}_{0}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int p_{0|t}(\bm{a}_{0}|\bm{a}_{t})d\bm{a}_{0}=1</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex28" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v\cdot 1=\int\bm{v}_{t}(\bm{a}_{t}|\bm{a}_{0})p_{0|t}(\bm{a}_{0}|\bm{a}_{t})\,d\bm{a}_{0}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒗</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v\cdot 1=\int\bm{v}_{t}(\bm{a}_{t}|\bm{a}_{0})p_{0|t}(\bm{a}_{0}|\bm{a}_{t})\,d\bm{a}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="A4.Ex29" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v^{*}=\mathbb{E}_{\bm{a}_{0}\sim p_{0|t}(\bm{a}_{0}|\bm{a}_{t})}[\bm{v}_{t}(\bm{a}_{t}|\bm{a}_{0})]" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒗</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v^{*}=\mathbb{E}_{\bm{a}_{0}\sim p_{0|t}(\bm{a}_{0}|\bm{a}_{t})}[\bm{v}_{t}(\bm{a}_{t}|\bm{a}_{0})]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS1.p4.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.p4.3.1" class="ltx_text">Finally, by definition, we know that the marginal velocity field <math id="A4.SS1.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{u}_{t}(\bm{x}_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝒖</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{u}_{t}(\bm{x}_{t})</annotation></semantics></math> is defined exactly by</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex30" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{u}_{t}\doteq\mathbb{E}_{\bm{a}_{0}\sim p_{0|t}(\bm{a}_{0}|\bm{a}_{t})}[\bm{v}_{t}(\bm{a}_{t}|\bm{a}_{0})]=v^{*}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝒖</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>≐</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒗</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{u}_{t}\doteq\mathbb{E}_{\bm{a}_{0}\sim p_{0|t}(\bm{a}_{0}|\bm{a}_{t})}[\bm{v}_{t}(\bm{a}_{t}|\bm{a}_{0})]=v^{*},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS1.p4.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.p4.4.1" class="ltx_text">which concludes the proof.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A4.Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_corollary">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Corollary D.2</span></span><span id="A4.Thmtheorem2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Diffusion marginal velocity field is the noisy score functions.)<span id="A4.Thmtheorem2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Specifically, for the VE diffusion models, the marginal velocity field is the score function of the perterubed data distribution, <em id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_upright">i.e.</em>,</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex31" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{u}_{t}(\bm{a}_{t})=\nabla_{\bm{a}_{t}}\log D_{\theta}(\bm{a}_{t};t)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝒖</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{u}_{t}(\bm{a}_{t})=\nabla_{\bm{a}_{t}}\log D_{\theta}(\bm{a}_{t};t)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">which is derived by</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex32" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex32X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex32X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\bm{u}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝒖</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\bm{u}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex32X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\doteq\mathbb{E}_{\bm{a}_{0}\sim p_{0|t}(\bm{a}_{0}|\bm{a}_{t})}[\bm{v}_{t}(\bm{a}_{t}|\bm{a}_{0})]=\int p_{0|t}(\bm{a}_{0}|\bm{a}_{t})\nabla\log p_{t|0}(\bm{a}_{t}|\bm{a}_{0})d\bm{a}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≐</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>𝒗</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo stretchy="false">]</mo><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo>∫</mo></mstyle><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>log</mi><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mi>d</mi><mi>𝒂</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\doteq\mathbb{E}_{\bm{a}_{0}\sim p_{0|t}(\bm{a}_{0}|\bm{a}_{t})}[\bm{v}_{t}(\bm{a}_{t}|\bm{a}_{0})]=\int p_{0|t}(\bm{a}_{0}|\bm{a}_{t})\nabla\log p_{t|0}(\bm{a}_{t}|\bm{a}_{0})d\bm{a}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex32Xa"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex32Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\int\frac{p_{t|0}(\bm{a}_{t}|\bm{a}_{0})\pi_{\rm old}(\bm{a}_{0})}{p_{t}(\bm{a}_{t})}\nabla\log p_{t|0}(\bm{a}_{t}|\bm{a}_{0})d\bm{a}_{0}=\frac{1}{p_{t}(\bm{a}_{t})}\int\pi_{\rm old}(\bm{a}_{0})\nabla p_{t|0}(\bm{a}_{t}|\bm{a}_{0})d\bm{a}_{0}=\frac{1}{p_{t}(\bm{a}_{t})}\nabla p_{t}(\bm{a}_{t})=\nabla\log p_{t}(\bm{a}_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo>∫</mo></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>old</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>log</mi><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mi>d</mi><mi>𝒂</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo>∫</mo></mstyle><mi>π</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>old</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mi>d</mi><mi>𝒂</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>=</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>log</mi><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\int\frac{p_{t|0}(\bm{a}_{t}|\bm{a}_{0})\pi_{\rm old}(\bm{a}_{0})}{p_{t}(\bm{a}_{t})}\nabla\log p_{t|0}(\bm{a}_{t}|\bm{a}_{0})d\bm{a}_{0}=\frac{1}{p_{t}(\bm{a}_{t})}\int\pi_{\rm old}(\bm{a}_{0})\nabla p_{t|0}(\bm{a}_{t}|\bm{a}_{0})d\bm{a}_{0}=\frac{1}{p_{t}(\bm{a}_{t})}\nabla p_{t}(\bm{a}_{t})=\nabla\log p_{t}(\bm{a}_{t})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.2 </span>Closed-Form Solution of Reweighted Conditional Flow Matching.</h3>

<div id="A4.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Then we show our main results about the reweighted conditional flow matching</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.Thmtheorem3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem D.3</span></span><span id="A4.Thmtheorem3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Optimal solution of the reweighted conditional flow matching.)<span id="A4.Thmtheorem3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A4.Thmtheorem3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.Thmtheorem3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">When <math id="A4.Thmtheorem3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{\bm{a}_{0}\sim p_{0|t}}[w(\bm{a}_{0})]&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>𝐚</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐚</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{\bm{a}_{0}\sim p_{0|t}}[w(\bm{a}_{0})]&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, the reweighted conditional flow matching loss</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex33" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{W}=\mathbb{E}_{t\sim\mathcal{U},\ \bm{a}_{0}\sim\pi_{\rm old}(\bm{a}_{0}),\ x\sim p_{t|0}(\bm{a}|\bm{a}_{0})}\left[w(\bm{a}_{0})\|D_{\theta}(\bm{a}_{t};t)-\bm{v}_{t}(\bm{a}_{t}|\bm{a}_{0})\|^{2}\right]" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>W</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒰</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.577em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>old</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.577em">,</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒗</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{W}=\mathbb{E}_{t\sim\mathcal{U},\ \bm{a}_{0}\sim\pi_{\rm old}(\bm{a}_{0}),\ x\sim p_{t|0}(\bm{a}|\bm{a}_{0})}\left[w(\bm{a}_{0})\|D_{\theta}(\bm{a}_{t};t)-\bm{v}_{t}(\bm{a}_{t}|\bm{a}_{0})\|^{2}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.Thmtheorem3.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem3.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">induces optimal solution</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex34" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex34.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{t}^{*}(\bm{a}_{t};t)=\frac{\mathbb{E}_{\bm{a}_{0}\sim p_{0|t}}[w(\bm{a}_{0})\bm{v}_{t}(\bm{a}_{t}|\bm{a}_{0})]}{\mathbb{E}_{\bm{a}_{0}\sim p_{0|t}}[w(\bm{a}_{0})]}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒗</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{t}^{*}(\bm{a}_{t};t)=\frac{\mathbb{E}_{\bm{a}_{0}\sim p_{0|t}}[w(\bm{a}_{0})\bm{v}_{t}(\bm{a}_{t}|\bm{a}_{0})]}{\mathbb{E}_{\bm{a}_{0}\sim p_{0|t}}[w(\bm{a}_{0})]}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Step 1: Rewrite as an Integral.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Expand the expectations into their integral forms:</p>
<table id="A4.Ex35" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex35.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{W}=\int_{0}^{1}\int\int\pi_{\rm old}(\bm{a}_{0})p_{t|0}(\bm{a}|\bm{a}_{0})w(\bm{a}_{0})\|D_{\theta}(\bm{a}_{t};t)-\bm{v}_{t}(\bm{a}_{t}|\bm{a}_{0})\|^{2}\,d\bm{a}_{0}\,d\bm{a}_{t}\,dt" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>W</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><mo>∫</mo></mrow><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>old</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒗</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{W}=\int_{0}^{1}\int\int\pi_{\rm old}(\bm{a}_{0})p_{t|0}(\bm{a}|\bm{a}_{0})w(\bm{a}_{0})\|D_{\theta}(\bm{a}_{t};t)-\bm{v}_{t}(\bm{a}_{t}|\bm{a}_{0})\|^{2}\,d\bm{a}_{0}\,d\bm{a}_{t}\,dt</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Step 2: Apply Bayes’ Rule.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS2.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Substitute the joint distribution <math id="A4.SS2.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\rm old}(\bm{a}_{0})p_{t|0}(\bm{a}|\bm{a}_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>old</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\rm old}(\bm{a}_{0})p_{t|0}(\bm{a}|\bm{a}_{0})</annotation></semantics></math> with the marginal-posterior decomposition <math id="A4.SS2.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{t}(\bm{a}_{t})p_{0|t}(\bm{a}_{0}|\bm{a}_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{t}(\bm{a}_{t})p_{0|t}(\bm{a}_{0}|\bm{a}_{t})</annotation></semantics></math>. Note that <math id="A4.SS2.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w(\bm{a}_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w(\bm{a}_{0})</annotation></semantics></math> remains attached to the inner integral over <math id="A4.SS2.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{a}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{a}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
<table id="A4.Ex36" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex36.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{W}=\int_{0}^{1}\int p_{t}(\bm{a}_{t})\left[\int p_{0|t}(\bm{a}_{0}|\bm{a}_{t})w(\bm{a}_{0})\|D_{\theta}(\bm{a}_{t};t)-\bm{v}_{t}(\bm{a}_{t}|\bm{a}_{0})\|^{2}\,d\bm{a}_{0}\right]\,d\bm{a}_{t}\,dt" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>W</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em">∫</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒗</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{W}=\int_{0}^{1}\int p_{t}(\bm{a}_{t})\left[\int p_{0|t}(\bm{a}_{0}|\bm{a}_{t})w(\bm{a}_{0})\|D_{\theta}(\bm{a}_{t};t)-\bm{v}_{t}(\bm{a}_{t}|\bm{a}_{0})\|^{2}\,d\bm{a}_{0}\right]\,d\bm{a}_{t}\,dt</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS2.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS2.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Step 3: Pointwise Minimization.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS2.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS2.p7.1" class="ltx_p">To minimize the global loss, we minimize the inner term (in square brackets) for every fixed point <math id="A4.SS2.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> and time <math id="A4.SS2.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="A4.SS2.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J_{W}(v)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>W</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J_{W}(v)</annotation></semantics></math> be this local weighted objective:</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS2.p8" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A4.Ex37" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex37.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J_{W}(v)=\int p_{0|t}(\bm{a}_{0}|\bm{a}_{t})w(\bm{a}_{0})\|v-\bm{v}_{t}(\bm{a}_{t}|\bm{a}_{0})\|^{2}\,d\bm{a}_{0}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>W</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒗</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J_{W}(v)=\int p_{0|t}(\bm{a}_{0}|\bm{a}_{t})w(\bm{a}_{0})\|v-\bm{v}_{t}(\bm{a}_{t}|\bm{a}_{0})\|^{2}\,d\bm{a}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS2.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS2.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Step 4: Solve for v</span>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS2.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS2.p10.1" class="ltx_p">Rewrite the pointwise loss function, we have</p>
<table id="A4.E21" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J_{W}(v)=\underbrace{\left(\int p_{0|t}(\bm{a}_{0}|\bm{a}_{t})w(\bm{a}_{0})\,d\bm{a}_{0}\right)}_{M(\bm{a}_{t})}\|v\|^{2}-2v^{T}\underbrace{\left(\int p_{0|t}(\bm{a}_{0}|\bm{a}_{t})w(\bm{a}_{0})\bm{v}_{t}(\bm{a}_{t}|\bm{a}_{0})\,d\bm{a}_{0}\right)}_{N(\bm{a}_{t})}+C" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>W</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em">∫</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>v</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em">∫</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒗</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></munder></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J_{W}(v)=\underbrace{\left(\int p_{0|t}(\bm{a}_{0}|\bm{a}_{t})w(\bm{a}_{0})\,d\bm{a}_{0}\right)}_{M(\bm{a}_{t})}\|v\|^{2}-2v^{T}\underbrace{\left(\int p_{0|t}(\bm{a}_{0}|\bm{a}_{t})w(\bm{a}_{0})\bm{v}_{t}(\bm{a}_{t}|\bm{a}_{0})\,d\bm{a}_{0}\right)}_{N(\bm{a}_{t})}+C</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(21)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS2.p11" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS2.p11.1" class="ltx_p">The closed-form optimal solution only exists when <math id="A4.SS2.p11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M(\bm{a}_{t})&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M(\bm{a}_{t})&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS2.p12" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS2.p12.1" class="ltx_p">Calculate the gradient with respect to <math id="A4.SS2.p12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> and set it to zero:</p>
<table id="A4.Ex38" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex38.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{v}J_{W}(v)=\int p_{0|t}(\bm{a}_{0}|\bm{a}_{t})w(\bm{a}_{0})\cdot 2(v-\bm{v}_{t}(\bm{a}_{t}|\bm{a}_{0}))\,d\bm{a}_{0}=0" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>v</mi></msub><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>W</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒗</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{v}J_{W}(v)=\int p_{0|t}(\bm{a}_{0}|\bm{a}_{t})w(\bm{a}_{0})\cdot 2(v-\bm{v}_{t}(\bm{a}_{t}|\bm{a}_{0}))\,d\bm{a}_{0}=0</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.p12.2" class="ltx_p">Distribute the terms. Note that <math id="A4.SS2.p12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> is constant with respect to the integral over <math id="A4.SS2.p12.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{a}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{a}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A4.Ex39" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex39.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v\int p_{0|t}(\bm{a}_{0}|\bm{a}_{t})w(\bm{a}_{0})\,d\bm{a}_{0}=\int p_{0|t}(\bm{a}_{0}|\bm{a}_{t})w(\bm{a}_{0})\bm{v}_{t}(\bm{a}_{t}|\bm{a}_{0})\,d\bm{a}_{0}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒗</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v\int p_{0|t}(\bm{a}_{0}|\bm{a}_{t})w(\bm{a}_{0})\,d\bm{a}_{0}=\int p_{0|t}(\bm{a}_{0}|\bm{a}_{t})w(\bm{a}_{0})\bm{v}_{t}(\bm{a}_{t}|\bm{a}_{0})\,d\bm{a}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.p12.3" class="ltx_p">Crucial Difference: In the unweighted case, the integral on the left side was <math id="A4.SS2.p12.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\int p_{0|t}(\bm{a}_{0}|\bm{a}_{t})d\bm{a}_{0}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int p_{0|t}(\bm{a}_{0}|\bm{a}_{t})d\bm{a}_{0}=1</annotation></semantics></math>. Here, the integral is over the weighted posterior, so it does not sum to 1. It acts as a normalizing constant for the weights.We solve for <math id="A4.SS2.p12.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A4.Ex40" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex40.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v=\frac{\int p_{0|t}(\bm{a}_{0}|\bm{a}_{t})w(\bm{a}_{0})\bm{v}_{t}(\bm{a}_{t}|\bm{a}_{0})\,d\bm{a}_{0}}{\int p_{0|t}(\bm{a}_{0}|\bm{a}_{t})w(\bm{a}_{0})\,d\bm{a}_{0}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒗</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v=\frac{\int p_{0|t}(\bm{a}_{0}|\bm{a}_{t})w(\bm{a}_{0})\bm{v}_{t}(\bm{a}_{t}|\bm{a}_{0})\,d\bm{a}_{0}}{\int p_{0|t}(\bm{a}_{0}|\bm{a}_{t})w(\bm{a}_{0})\,d\bm{a}_{0}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.p12.4" class="ltx_p">Rearrange it we get the optimal solution,</p>
<table id="A4.Ex41" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex41.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{t}^{*}(\bm{a}_{t})=\frac{\mathbb{E}_{\bm{a}_{0}\sim p_{0|t}}[w(\bm{a}_{0})\bm{v}_{t}(\bm{a}_{t}|\bm{a}_{0})]}{\mathbb{E}_{\bm{a}_{0}\sim p_{0|t}}[w(\bm{a}_{0})]}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒗</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{t}^{*}(\bm{a}_{t})=\frac{\mathbb{E}_{\bm{a}_{0}\sim p_{0|t}}[w(\bm{a}_{0})\bm{v}_{t}(\bm{a}_{t}|\bm{a}_{0})]}{\mathbb{E}_{\bm{a}_{0}\sim p_{0|t}}[w(\bm{a}_{0})]}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.3 </span>Velocity field generates reweighted data distribution.</h3>

<div id="A4.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We aim to derive</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">In <span id="A4.SS3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Case I</span> when <math id="A4.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{a}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{a}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies <math id="A4.SS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{\bm{a}_{0}\sim p_{0|t}(\cdot|\bm{a}_{t})}[w(\bm{s},\bm{a}_{0})]&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>𝒂</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∼</mo><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>w</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{\bm{a}_{0}\sim p_{0|t}(\cdot|\bm{a}_{t})}[w(\bm{s},\bm{a}_{0})]&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, the closed-form velocity field solution <a href="#S3.E8" title="In 3.1 A Two-Stage Framework for Diffusion Policy Optimization ‣ 3 A Unified Framework for Reweighting with Measure Matching ‣ SiMPO: Measure Matching for Online Diffusion Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Equation</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a> generate probability path</p>
<table id="A4.Ex42" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex42.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{t}(\bm{a}|\bm{s})=\frac{1}{Z}\int w(\bm{s},\bm{a}_{0})\pi_{\rm old}(\bm{a}_{0}|\bm{s})p_{t|0}(\bm{a}|\bm{a}_{0})\,d\bm{a}_{0}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>Z</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>old</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{t}(\bm{a}|\bm{s})=\frac{1}{Z}\int w(\bm{s},\bm{a}_{0})\pi_{\rm old}(\bm{a}_{0}|\bm{s})p_{t|0}(\bm{a}|\bm{a}_{0})\,d\bm{a}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.p2.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A4.SS3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z(\bm{s})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z(\bm{s})</annotation></semantics></math> is the global normalizing constant: <math id="A4.SS3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z=\int w(\bm{s},\bm{a}_{0})\pi_{\rm old}(\bm{a}_{0}|\bm{s})\,d\bm{a}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>old</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z=\int w(\bm{s},\bm{a}_{0})\pi_{\rm old}(\bm{a}_{0}|\bm{s})\,d\bm{a}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS3.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A4.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">To prove <math id="A4.SS3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{t}^{*}(\bm{a};t)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{t}^{*}(\bm{a};t)</annotation></semantics></math> generates this distribution, we just need to verify that it satisfies the Continuity Equation (Conservation of Mass) for <math id="A4.SS3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{t}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{t}(x)</annotation></semantics></math>.The continuity equation states:</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex43" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex43.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\partial\rho_{t}}{\partial t}+\nabla\cdot(\rho_{t}v_{t}^{*})=0" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo>∇</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\partial\rho_{t}}{\partial t}+\nabla\cdot(\rho_{t}v_{t}^{*})=0</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS3.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS3.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Step A: Expand the Divergence Term.<span id="A4.SS3.p4.1.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span></span></p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS3.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS3.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let’s look at the flow term <math id="A4.SS3.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{t}v_{t}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{t}v_{t}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>. Substituting your definition of the optimal solution:</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex44" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex44.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{t}^{*}(\bm{a}_{t})=\frac{\mathbb{E}_{p_{0|t}}[w\bm{v}]}{\mathbb{E}_{p_{0|t}}[w]}=\frac{\int w(\bm{a}_{0})p_{t|0}(\bm{a}_{t}|\bm{a}_{0})\pi_{\rm old}(\bm{a}_{0})\bm{v}_{t}(\bm{a}_{t}|\bm{a}_{0})d\bm{a}_{0}}{\int w(\bm{a}_{0})p_{t|0}(\bm{a}_{t}|\bm{a}_{0})\pi_{\rm old}(\bm{a}_{0})d\bm{a}_{0}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒗</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>w</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>old</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒗</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>old</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{t}^{*}(\bm{a}_{t})=\frac{\mathbb{E}_{p_{0|t}}[w\bm{v}]}{\mathbb{E}_{p_{0|t}}[w]}=\frac{\int w(\bm{a}_{0})p_{t|0}(\bm{a}_{t}|\bm{a}_{0})\pi_{\rm old}(\bm{a}_{0})\bm{v}_{t}(\bm{a}_{t}|\bm{a}_{0})d\bm{a}_{0}}{\int w(\bm{a}_{0})p_{t|0}(\bm{a}_{t}|\bm{a}_{0})\pi_{\rm old}(\bm{a}_{0})d\bm{a}_{0}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">The denominator is exactly the unnormalized density, let’s call it <math id="A4.SS3.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\rho}_{t}(x)=Z\rho_{t}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ρ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\rho}_{t}(x)=Z\rho_{t}(x)</annotation></semantics></math>.So, <math id="A4.SS3.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\rho}_{t}(x)v_{t}^{*}(\bm{a}_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ρ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\rho}_{t}(x)v_{t}^{*}(\bm{a}_{t})</annotation></semantics></math> is just the numerator:</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex45" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex45.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\rho}_{t}v_{t}^{*}=\int w(\bm{a}_{0})\pi_{\rm old}(\bm{a}_{0})\left[p_{t|0}(\bm{a}_{t}|\bm{a}_{0})\bm{v}_{t}(\bm{a}_{t}|\bm{a}_{0})\right]\,d\bm{a}_{0}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ρ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>old</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒗</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\rho}_{t}v_{t}^{*}=\int w(\bm{a}_{0})\pi_{\rm old}(\bm{a}_{0})\left[p_{t|0}(\bm{a}_{t}|\bm{a}_{0})\bm{v}_{t}(\bm{a}_{t}|\bm{a}_{0})\right]\,d\bm{a}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.p5.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p5.3.1" class="ltx_text">Step B: Apply Divergence</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex46" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex46.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla\cdot(\tilde{\rho}_{t}v_{t}^{*})=\int w(\bm{a}_{0})\pi_{\rm old}(\bm{a}_{0})\underbrace{\nabla\cdot(p_{t|0}(\bm{a}_{t}|\bm{a}_{0})\bm{v}_{t}(\bm{a}_{t}|\bm{a}_{0}))}_{\text{Conditional Continuity}}\,d\bm{a}_{0}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>∇</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ρ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>old</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mo>∇</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒗</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><mtext>Conditional Continuity</mtext></munder><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla\cdot(\tilde{\rho}_{t}v_{t}^{*})=\int w(\bm{a}_{0})\pi_{\rm old}(\bm{a}_{0})\underbrace{\nabla\cdot(p_{t|0}(\bm{a}_{t}|\bm{a}_{0})\bm{v}_{t}(\bm{a}_{t}|\bm{a}_{0}))}_{\text{Conditional Continuity}}\,d\bm{a}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.p5.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p5.4.1" class="ltx_text">We know that for the conditional path (e.g., Gaussian), the conditional velocity <math id="A4.SS3.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{u}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝒖</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{u}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies continuity:<math id="A4.SS3.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla\cdot(pu)=-\frac{\partial p}{\partial t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>∇</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla\cdot(pu)=-\frac{\partial p}{\partial t}</annotation></semantics></math>.Substitute this back:</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex47" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex47.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla\cdot(\tilde{\rho}_{t}v_{t}^{*})=\int w(\bm{a}_{0})\pi_{\rm old}(\bm{a}_{0})\left(-\frac{\partial p_{t|0}(\bm{a}_{t}|\bm{a}_{0})}{\partial t}\right)\,d\bm{a}_{0}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>∇</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ρ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>old</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla\cdot(\tilde{\rho}_{t}v_{t}^{*})=\int w(\bm{a}_{0})\pi_{\rm old}(\bm{a}_{0})\left(-\frac{\partial p_{t|0}(\bm{a}_{t}|\bm{a}_{0})}{\partial t}\right)\,d\bm{a}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.p5.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p5.5.1" class="ltx_text">Step C: Linearity of the DerivativePull the derivative and negative sign out:</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex48" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex48.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\nabla\cdot(\tilde{\rho}_{t}v_{t}^{*})=-\frac{\partial}{\partial t}\int w(\bm{a}_{0})\pi_{\rm old}(\bm{a}_{0})p_{t|0}(\bm{a}_{t}|\bm{a}_{0})\,d\bm{a}_{0}=-\frac{\partial\tilde{\rho}_{t}}{\partial t}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>∇</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ρ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mfrac><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>∫</mo><mi>w</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>old</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ρ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla\cdot(\tilde{\rho}_{t}v_{t}^{*})=-\frac{\partial}{\partial t}\int w(\bm{a}_{0})\pi_{\rm old}(\bm{a}_{0})p_{t|0}(\bm{a}_{t}|\bm{a}_{0})\,d\bm{a}_{0}=-\frac{\partial\tilde{\rho}_{t}}{\partial t}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.p5.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p5.6.1" class="ltx_text">Result:</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex49" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex49.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\partial\tilde{\rho}_{t}}{\partial t}+\nabla\cdot(\tilde{\rho}_{t}v_{t}^{*})=0" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ρ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo>∇</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>ρ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\partial\tilde{\rho}_{t}}{\partial t}+\nabla\cdot(\tilde{\rho}_{t}v_{t}^{*})=0</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.p5.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p5.7.1" class="ltx_text">This confirms that the vector field indeed evolves the initial distribution <math id="A4.SS3.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{0}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{0}(x)</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A4.SS3.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{1}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{1}(x)</annotation></semantics></math> according to the laws of probability flow.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS3.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS3.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.4 </span>Cases when <math id="A4.SS4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{\bm{a}_{0}\sim p_{0|t}}[w(\bm{a}_{0})]\leqslant 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{\bm{a}_{0}\sim p_{0|t}}[w(\bm{a}_{0})]\leqslant 0</annotation></semantics></math>.</h3>

<div id="A4.Thmtheorem4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_corollary">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Corollary D.4</span></span><span id="A4.Thmtheorem4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A4.Thmtheorem4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.Thmtheorem4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">When <math id="A4.Thmtheorem4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{\bm{a}_{0}\sim p_{0|t}}[w(\bm{a}_{0})]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>𝐚</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo fence="false">|</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐚</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{\bm{a}_{0}\sim p_{0|t}}[w(\bm{a}_{0})]</annotation></semantics></math>, the loss in (<a href="#A4.E21" title="Equation 21 ‣ D.2 Closed-Form Solution of Reweighted Conditional Flow Matching. ‣ Appendix D Derivation of Closed-Form Solution of Reweighted Conditional Flow Matching. ‣ SiMPO: Measure Matching for Online Diffusion Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">21</span></a>) is unbounded and the gradient push <math id="A4.Thmtheorem4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> away from</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS4.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A4.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">the <a href="#A4.E21" title="In D.2 Closed-Form Solution of Reweighted Conditional Flow Matching. ‣ Appendix D Derivation of Closed-Form Solution of Reweighted Conditional Flow Matching. ‣ SiMPO: Measure Matching for Online Diffusion Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Equation</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">21</span></a> can be rewritten by <math id="A4.SS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M(\bm{a}_{t})\|v\|^{2}-2N(\bm{a}_{t}))^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">OPEN</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒂</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M(\bm{a}_{t})\|v\|^{2}-2N(\bm{a}_{t}))^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A5" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix E </span>Derivation of Closed-Form Solutions for Linear and Square Weighting</h2>

<div id="A5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we derive the closed-form solutions for the scalar <math id="A5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> under two common constraints involving the Rectified Linear Unit (ReLU). We consider a batch of samples <math id="A5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{x_{i}\}_{i=1}^{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{x_{i}\}_{i=1}^{N}</annotation></semantics></math> and a scaling parameter <math id="A5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>l</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<section id="A5.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">E.1 </span>General Setup and Notation</h3>

<div id="A5.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We sort the samples in descending order such that <math id="A5.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{(1)}\geqslant x_{(2)}\geqslant\dots\geqslant x_{(N)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>⩾</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>⩾</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">⋯</mi><mo>⩾</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{(1)}\geqslant x_{(2)}\geqslant\dots\geqslant x_{(N)}</annotation></semantics></math>.
We define the <span id="A5.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">active set</span> <math id="A5.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math> as the set of indices where the ReLU term is non-zero, i.e., <math id="A5.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S=\{i\mid x_{i}&gt;v\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>i</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S=\{i\mid x_{i}&gt;v\}</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="A5.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=|S|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=|S|</annotation></semantics></math> denote the number of active samples. For <math id="A5.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in S</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A5.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{ReLU}(x_{i}-v)=x_{i}-v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mtext>ReLU</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{ReLU}(x_{i}-v)=x_{i}-v</annotation></semantics></math>; otherwise, it is 0.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Because the objective functions in both cases are monotonic with respect to <math id="A5.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math>, we can determine the optimal active set size <math id="A5.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> efficiently by checking conditions on the sorted samples.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A5.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">E.2 </span>Case 1: Linear Constraint</h3>

<div id="A5.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We first consider the linear constraint:</p>
<table id="A5.E22" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.E22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\frac{\text{ReLU}(x_{i}-v)}{l}=1." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover><mfrac><mrow><mtext>ReLU</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>l</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\frac{\text{ReLU}(x_{i}-v)}{l}=1.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(22)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Rearranging, we require the sum of active excesses to equal the target mass <math id="A5.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{1}=N\cdot l" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{1}=N\cdot l</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A5.E23" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.E23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{i\in S}(x_{i}-v)=C_{1}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{i\in S}(x_{i}-v)=C_{1}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(23)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Solving for <math id="A5.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> yields the solution:</p>
<table id="A5.E24" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.E24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v=\frac{1}{k}\left(\sum_{i\in S}x_{i}-C_{1}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>k</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></munder><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v=\frac{1}{k}\left(\sum_{i\in S}x_{i}-C_{1}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(24)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS2.p1.4" class="ltx_p">To determine <math id="A5.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>, we find the largest index <math id="A5.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> such that the “excess mass” at the boundary <math id="A5.SS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{(k)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{(k)}</annotation></semantics></math> is strictly less than the target <math id="A5.SS2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A5.E25" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.E25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{j=1}^{k}(x_{(j)}-x_{(k)})&lt;N\cdot l." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>k</mi></munderover><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{j=1}^{k}(x_{(j)}-x_{(k)})&lt;N\cdot l.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(25)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A5.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">E.3 </span>Case 2: Squared Constraint</h3>

<div id="A5.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Next, we consider the squared constraint:</p>
<table id="A5.E26" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.E26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\left(\frac{\text{ReLU}(x_{i}-v)}{l}\right)^{2}=1." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mtext>ReLU</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>l</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\left(\frac{\text{ReLU}(x_{i}-v)}{l}\right)^{2}=1.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(26)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A5.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{2}=N\cdot l^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>l</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{2}=N\cdot l^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. Expanding the square over the active set <math id="A5.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math>, we obtain a quadratic equation in <math id="A5.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A5.EGx1" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.Ex50"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell" style="padding-top:0.5pt;padding-bottom:0.5pt;"><math id="A5.Ex50.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{i\in S}(x_{i}-v)^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{i\in S}(x_{i}-v)^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell" style="padding-top:0.5pt;padding-bottom:0.5pt;"><math id="A5.Ex50.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=C_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=C_{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.E27"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell" style="padding-top:0.5pt;padding-bottom:0.5pt;"><math id="A5.E27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle kv^{2}-2\left(\sum_{i\in S}x_{i}\right)v+\left(\sum_{i\in S}x_{i}^{2}-C_{2}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle kv^{2}-2\left(\sum_{i\in S}x_{i}\right)v+\left(\sum_{i\in S}x_{i}^{2}-C_{2}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell" style="padding-top:0.5pt;padding-bottom:0.5pt;"><math id="A5.E27.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=0." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(27)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS3.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Using the quadratic formula and selecting the negative root (since <math id="A5.SS3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> acts as a lower cutoff and must satisfy <math id="A5.SS3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v&lt;\frac{1}{k}\sum x_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>k</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>∑</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v&lt;\frac{1}{k}\sum x_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> to generate variance), we obtain:</p>
<table id="A5.E28" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.E28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v=\frac{1}{k}\left(\sum_{i\in S}x_{i}-\sqrt{\left(\sum_{i\in S}x_{i}\right)^{2}-k\left(\sum_{i\in S}x_{i}^{2}-C_{2}\right)}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>k</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></munder><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><msqrt><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></munder><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></munder><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v=\frac{1}{k}\left(\sum_{i\in S}x_{i}-\sqrt{\left(\sum_{i\in S}x_{i}\right)^{2}-k\left(\sum_{i\in S}x_{i}^{2}-C_{2}\right)}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(28)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS3.p1.4" class="ltx_p">To determine <math id="A5.SS3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> in this case, we compute the “energy at the boundary” <math id="A5.SS3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> for the candidate cutoff <math id="A5.SS3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{(k)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{(k)}</annotation></semantics></math> and select the largest <math id="A5.SS3.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="A5.SS3.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{k}&lt;C_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{k}&lt;C_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A5.E29" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.E29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{k}=\sum_{j=1}^{k}(x_{(j)}-x_{(k)})^{2}&lt;N\cdot l^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>k</mi></munderover><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mi>l</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{k}=\sum_{j=1}^{k}(x_{(j)}-x_{(k)})^{2}&lt;N\cdot l^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(29)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A5.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">E.4 </span>Reference Implementation</h3>

<div id="A5.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We provide a vectorized JAX implementation for solving both the linear and squared constraints derived in Section <a href="#A5" title="Appendix E Derivation of Closed-Form Solutions for Linear and Square Weighting ‣ SiMPO: Measure Matching for Online Diffusion Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">E</span></a>. This implementation supports batch processing and is differentiable.</p>
</div>
<figure id="LST1" class="ltx_float ltx_lstlisting">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
<p id="LST1.2" class="ltx_p ltx_figure_panel">JAX implementation for solving <math id="LST1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math>.</p></div><div class="ltx_flex_break"></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
<div id="LST1.3" class="ltx_listing ltx_figure_panel ltx_lst_language_Python ltx_lstlisting ltx_framed ltx_framed_rectangle ltx_listing"><div class="ltx_listing_data"><a href="data:text/plain;base64," download="">⬇</a></div>
