</section>
</section>
<section id="A6" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix F </span>Experimental Details</h2>

<section id="A6.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">F.1 </span>Baselines</h3>

<div id="A6.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We evaluate our approach against two distinct families of reinforcement learning (RL) algorithms. The first group consists of five state-of-the-art <span id="A6.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">online diffusion-policy methods</span>, encompassing both off-policy and on-policy architectures:</p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<ul id="A6.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A6.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A6.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">QSM</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib47" title="" class="ltx_ref">Psenka et al., 2023</a>)</cite>: Implements Langevin dynamics using the gradient of a learned <math id="A6.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q</annotation></semantics></math>-function as the score function.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A6.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A6.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">QVPO</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib50" title="" class="ltx_ref">Ding et al., 2024</a>)</cite>: Employs a <math id="A6.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q</annotation></semantics></math>-weighted variational objective for diffusion training, though it is notably constrained by its inability to process negative rewards effectively.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A6.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A6.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">DACER</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib52" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wang et al., 2024b</a>)</cite>: Backpropagates gradients directly through the reverse diffusion process and utilizes a GMM entropy regulator to manage the exploration-exploitation trade-off.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A6.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A6.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.I1.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">DIPO</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib49" title="" class="ltx_ref">Yang et al., 2023</a>)</cite>: Uses a two-stage approach where state-action particles are updated via <math id="A6.I1.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q</annotation></semantics></math>-gradients before being fitted to a diffusion model.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A6.I1.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A6.I1.i5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.I1.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.I1.i5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">DPPO</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib54" title="" class="ltx_ref">Ren et al., 2024</a>)</cite>: Formulates a dual-layer MDP spanning diffusion and environment steps, optimized via Proximal Policy Optimization. We employ the training-from-scratch configuration to maintain a fair comparison with other methods.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">The second group includes three <span id="A6.SS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">classic model-free baselines</span>: <span id="A6.SS1.p3.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">PPO</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib56" title="" class="ltx_ref">Schulman et al., 2017</a>)</cite>, <span id="A6.SS1.p3.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">TD3</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib58" title="" class="ltx_ref">Fujimoto et al., 2018</a>)</cite>, and <span id="A6.SS1.p3.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">SAC</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib48" title="" class="ltx_ref">Haarnoja et al., 2018</a>)</cite>. For PPO, we utilize a buffer size of 4096 and perform 10 gradient updates per sample. Across all baselines, we collect samples from 5 parallel environments for a total of 1 million environment interactions and 200k iterations. Performance is reported as the average return over 20 episodes across 5 random seeds.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A6.T4" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="A6.T4.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 4</span>: </span><span id="A6.T4.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Hyperparameters</span></figcaption>
<table id="A6.T4.5" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="A6.T4.5.1" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A6.T4.5.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_r ltx_border_tt"><span id="A6.T4.5.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Name</span></th>
<td id="A6.T4.5.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt"><span id="A6.T4.5.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Value</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A6.T4.5.2" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A6.T4.5.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_r ltx_border_t">Critic learning rate</th>
<td id="A6.T4.5.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t">3e-4</td></tr>
<tr id="A6.T4.5.3" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A6.T4.5.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_r">Policy learning rate</th>
<td id="A6.T4.5.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">3e-4, linear annealing to 3e-5</td></tr>
<tr id="A6.T4.5.4" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A6.T4.5.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_r">Diffusion steps</th>
<td id="A6.T4.5.4.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">20</td></tr>
<tr id="A6.T4.5.5" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A6.T4.5.5.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_r">Diffusion noise schedules</th>
<td id="A6.T4.5.5.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">Cosine</td></tr>
<tr id="A6.T4.5.6" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A6.T4.5.6.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_r">Policy network hidden layers</th>
<td id="A6.T4.5.6.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">3</td></tr>
<tr id="A6.T4.5.7" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A6.T4.5.7.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_r">Policy network hidden neurons</th>
<td id="A6.T4.5.7.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">256</td></tr>
<tr id="A6.T4.5.8" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A6.T4.5.8.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_r">Policy network activation</th>
<td id="A6.T4.5.8.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">Mish</td></tr>
<tr id="A6.T4.5.9" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A6.T4.5.9.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_r">Value network hidden layers</th>
<td id="A6.T4.5.9.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">3</td></tr>
<tr id="A6.T4.5.10" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A6.T4.5.10.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_r">Value network hidden neurons</th>
<td id="A6.T4.5.10.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">256</td></tr>
<tr id="A6.T4.5.11" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A6.T4.5.11.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_r">Value network activation</th>
<td id="A6.T4.5.11.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">Mish</td></tr>
<tr id="A6.T4.5.12" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A6.T4.5.12.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_bb ltx_border_r">replay buffer size (off-policy only)</th>
<td id="A6.T4.5.12.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb">1 million</td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</figure>
<div id="A6.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">where the Cosine noise schedule means
<math id="A6.SS1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{t}=1-\frac{\bar{\alpha}_{t}}{\alpha_{t-1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><msub><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{t}=1-\frac{\bar{\alpha}_{t}}{\alpha_{t-1}}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A6.SS1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{\alpha}_{t}=\frac{f(t)}{f(0)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{\alpha}_{t}=\frac{f(t)}{f(0)}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A6.SS1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(t)=\cos\left(\frac{t/T+s}{1+s}*\frac{\pi}{2}\right)^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo>⁡</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∗</mo><mfrac><mi>π</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(t)=\cos\left(\frac{t/T+s}{1+s}*\frac{\pi}{2}\right)^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS1.p5.1" class="ltx_p">To provide a formal mathematical summary of the reward functions for your paper, you can use the following LaTeX code. It uses the amsmath package for aligned equations and a table for comparison.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A6.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">F.2 </span>Reward Functions</h3>

<div id="A6.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The Cheetah domain tasks are designed to track a target horizontal velocity <math id="A6.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v^{*}=10.0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>10.0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v^{*}=10.0</annotation></semantics></math> m/s (limited by the physical capability, the robot cannot actually achieve 10m/s. Therefore, the task is to run as fast as possible.). Let <math id="A6.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> denote the current horizontal velocity of the torso. We evaluate our method across several reward formulations, categorized into linear, quadratic, and absolute value variations.</p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We design the following reward functions (with proper transformation to align the scale), ranked from “flat” landscape to “steep” landscape,</p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<ul id="A6.I2" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A6.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A6.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.I2.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Sqrt</span> reward
<math id="A6.I2.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{abs\_sqrt}(v)=\sqrt{|v-v^{*}|}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>_</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{abs\_sqrt}(v)=\sqrt{|v-v^{*}|}</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A6.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A6.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.I2.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Linear</span> reward <math id="A6.I2.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{\rm linear}(v)=\frac{v}{v^{*}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>linear</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>v</mi><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{\rm linear}(v)=\frac{v}{v^{*}}</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A6.I2.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A6.I2.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.I2.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.I2.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Square</span> reward
<math id="A6.I2.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{abs\_sq}(v)=|v-v^{*}|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>_</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{abs\_sq}(v)=|v-v^{*}|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A6.I2.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A6.I2.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.I2.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.I2.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Exponental</span> reward
<math id="A6.I2.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{abs\_exp}(v)=\exp(-|v-v^{*}|)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>_</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{abs\_exp}(v)=\exp(-|v-v^{*}|)</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A7" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix G </span>Automatic temperature tuning</h2>

<div id="A7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib42" title="" class="ltx_ref">Abdolmaleki et al. (2018)</a></cite> shows that we can tun the temperature variable <math id="A7.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math> in <a href="#S3.E4" title="In 3.1 A Two-Stage Framework for Diffusion Policy Optimization ‣ 3 A Unified Framework for Reweighting with Measure Matching ‣ SiMPO: Measure Matching for Online Diffusion Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Equation</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> by primal-dual optimization, where the dual loss to update <math id="A7.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math> is</p>
<table id="A7.E30" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.E30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda\epsilon+\lambda\operatorname{logsumexp}(\frac{Q(s,a^{i})}{\lambda})-\lambda\log N" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>logsumexp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>λ</mi></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda\epsilon+\lambda\operatorname{logsumexp}(\frac{Q(s,a^{i})}{\lambda})-\lambda\log N</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(30)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A7.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.p2.1" class="ltx_p">First we compute the gradient of the second term,
Let <math id="A7.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(\lambda)=\lambda\cdot\operatorname{logsumexp}(Q/\lambda)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>logsumexp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(\lambda)=\lambda\cdot\operatorname{logsumexp}(Q/\lambda)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A7.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A7.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma G.1</span></span><span id="A7.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A7.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The gradient of <math id="A7.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(\lambda)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(\lambda)</annotation></semantics></math> with respect to <math id="A7.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math> is the Shannon entropy of the softmax distribution derived from <math id="A7.Thmtheorem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q</annotation></semantics></math>, i.e.,</span></p>
<table id="A7.Ex51" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.Ex51.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\partial f(\lambda)}{\partial\lambda}=\sum_{i}p_{i}-\log p_{i}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>i</mi></munder><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\partial f(\lambda)}{\partial\lambda}=\sum_{i}p_{i}-\log p_{i}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A7.Thmtheorem1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.Thmtheorem1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="A7.Thmtheorem1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{i}=\operatorname{softmax}(q_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>softmax</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{i}=\operatorname{softmax}(q_{i})</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A7.Thmtheorem1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{i}=Q(s,a^{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{i}=Q(s,a^{i})</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A7.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A7.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">1. Define the Function<span id="A7.p3.1.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span></span></p>
</div>
<div id="A7.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let the vector <math id="A7.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q=\left[q_{1},q_{2},\ldots,q_{N}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q=\left[q_{1},q_{2},\ldots,q_{N}\right]</annotation></semantics></math>. The function is:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A7.p5" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A7.Ex52" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.Ex52.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(\lambda)=\lambda\log\left(\sum_{i=1}^{N}\exp\left(\frac{q_{i}}{\lambda}\right)\right)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mi>λ</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(\lambda)=\lambda\log\left(\sum_{i=1}^{N}\exp\left(\frac{q_{i}}{\lambda}\right)\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A7.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">2. Differentiate with Respect to <math id="A7.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math></span></p>
</div>
<div id="A7.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">We use the product rule <math id="A7.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{d}{dx}[u\cdot v]=u^{\prime}v+uv^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>u</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{d}{dx}[u\cdot v]=u^{\prime}v+uv^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="A7.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z=\sum_{i=1}^{N}\exp\left(q_{i}/\lambda\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z=\sum_{i=1}^{N}\exp\left(q_{i}/\lambda\right)</annotation></semantics></math>. Then <math id="A7.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(\lambda)=\lambda\log(Z)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(\lambda)=\lambda\log(Z)</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A7.p8" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A7.Ex53" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.Ex53.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{gathered}\frac{\partial f}{\partial\lambda}=\frac{d}{d\lambda}[\lambda]\cdot\log(Z)+\lambda\cdot\frac{d}{d\lambda}[\log(Z)]\\
\frac{\partial f}{\partial\lambda}=1\cdot\log(Z)+\lambda\cdot\frac{1}{Z}\cdot\frac{\partial Z}{\partial\lambda}\end{gathered}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable displaystyle="true" rowspacing="1.0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>Z</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{gathered}\frac{\partial f}{\partial\lambda}=\frac{d}{d\lambda}[\lambda]\cdot\log(Z)+\lambda\cdot\frac{d}{d\lambda}[\log(Z)]\\
\frac{\partial f}{\partial\lambda}=1\cdot\log(Z)+\lambda\cdot\frac{1}{Z}\cdot\frac{\partial Z}{\partial\lambda}\end{gathered}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A7.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text">Next, we calculate <math id="A7.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\partial Z}{\partial\lambda}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\partial Z}{\partial\lambda}</annotation></semantics></math> :</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A7.p10" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A7.Ex54" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.Ex54.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\partial Z}{\partial\lambda}=\sum_{i=1}^{N}\frac{\partial}{\partial\lambda}\exp\left(q_{i}\lambda^{-1}\right)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover><mrow><mfrac><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\partial Z}{\partial\lambda}=\sum_{i=1}^{N}\frac{\partial}{\partial\lambda}\exp\left(q_{i}\lambda^{-1}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A7.p10.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.p10.1.1" class="ltx_text">Using the chain rule:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A7.p11" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A7.Ex55" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.Ex55.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\partial Z}{\partial\lambda}=\sum_{i=1}^{N}\exp\left(\frac{q_{i}}{\lambda}\right)\cdot\left(-\frac{q_{i}}{\lambda^{2}}\right)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mi>λ</mi></mfrac><mo rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><msup><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\partial Z}{\partial\lambda}=\sum_{i=1}^{N}\exp\left(\frac{q_{i}}{\lambda}\right)\cdot\left(-\frac{q_{i}}{\lambda^{2}}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A7.p12" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.p12.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.p12.1.1" class="ltx_text">3. Substitute and Simplify</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A7.p13" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.p13.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.p13.1.1" class="ltx_text">Substitute <math id="A7.p13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\partial Z}{\partial\lambda}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\partial Z}{\partial\lambda}</annotation></semantics></math> back into the main equation:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A7.p14" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A7.Ex56" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.Ex56.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{gathered}\frac{\partial f}{\partial\lambda}=\log(Z)+\frac{\lambda}{Z}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\exp\left(\frac{q_{i}}{\lambda}\right)\left(-\frac{q_{i}}{\lambda^{2}}\right)\\
\frac{\partial f}{\partial\lambda}=\log(Z)-\frac{1}{\lambda}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\frac{\exp\left(q_{i}/\lambda\right)}{Z}q_{i}\end{gathered}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable displaystyle="true" rowspacing="1.0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>λ</mi><mi>Z</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mi>λ</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><msup><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>λ</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>Z</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{gathered}\frac{\partial f}{\partial\lambda}=\log(Z)+\frac{\lambda}{Z}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\exp\left(\frac{q_{i}}{\lambda}\right)\left(-\frac{q_{i}}{\lambda^{2}}\right)\\
\frac{\partial f}{\partial\lambda}=\log(Z)-\frac{1}{\lambda}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\frac{\exp\left(q_{i}/\lambda\right)}{Z}q_{i}\end{gathered}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A7.p15" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.p15.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.p15.1.1" class="ltx_text">4. Interpretation as Entropy</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A7.p16" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.p16.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.p16.1.1" class="ltx_text">We can express this result using the softmax probabilities <math id="A7.p16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, where:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A7.p17" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A7.Ex57" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.Ex57.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{i}=\frac{\exp\left(q_{i}/\lambda\right)}{Z}=\frac{\exp\left(q_{i}/\lambda\right)}{\sum_{j}\exp\left(q_{j}/\lambda\right)}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>Z</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>j</mi></msub><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{i}=\frac{\exp\left(q_{i}/\lambda\right)}{Z}=\frac{\exp\left(q_{i}/\lambda\right)}{\sum_{j}\exp\left(q_{j}/\lambda\right)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A7.p18" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.p18.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.p18.1.1" class="ltx_text">Substituting <math id="A7.p18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> into the gradient:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A7.p19" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A7.Ex58" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.Ex58.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\partial f}{\partial\lambda}=\log(Z)-\frac{1}{\lambda}\sum_{i=1}^{N}p_{i}q_{i}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>λ</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\partial f}{\partial\lambda}=\log(Z)-\frac{1}{\lambda}\sum_{i=1}^{N}p_{i}q_{i}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A7.p20" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.p20.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.p20.1.1" class="ltx_text">To see why this is entropy, recall that <math id="A7.p20.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="H(p)=-\sum p_{i}\log\left(p_{i}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.055em">−</mo><mo>∑</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mi>log</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H(p)=-\sum p_{i}\log\left(p_{i}\right)</annotation></semantics></math>. Since <math id="A7.p20.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log\left(p_{i}\right)=\frac{q_{i}}{\lambda}-\log(Z)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mi>λ</mi></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log\left(p_{i}\right)=\frac{q_{i}}{\lambda}-\log(Z)</annotation></semantics></math>, we have:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A7.p21" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A7.Ex59" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.Ex59.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{gathered}H(p)=-\sum_{i=1}^{N}p_{i}\left(\frac{q_{i}}{\lambda}-\log(Z)\right)\\
H(p)=-\frac{1}{\lambda}\sum_{i=1}^{N}p_{i}q_{i}+\log(Z)\sum_{i=1}^{N}p_{i}\end{gathered}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable displaystyle="true" rowspacing="1.0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.055em">−</mo><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>N</mi></msup><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>(</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mi>λ</mi></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mi>log</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>)</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>λ</mi></mfrac><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>N</mi></msup><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mi>q</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>log</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>N</mi></msup><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{gathered}H(p)=-\sum_{i=1}^{N}p_{i}\left(\frac{q_{i}}{\lambda}-\log(Z)\right)\\
H(p)=-\frac{1}{\lambda}\sum_{i=1}^{N}p_{i}q_{i}+\log(Z)\sum_{i=1}^{N}p_{i}\end{gathered}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A7.p22" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.p22.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.p22.1.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="A7.p22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum p_{i}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>∑</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum p_{i}=1</annotation></semantics></math> :</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A7.p23" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A7.Ex60" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.Ex60.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H(p)=\log(Z)-\frac{1}{\lambda}\sum_{i=1}^{N}p_{i}q_{i}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>λ</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H(p)=\log(Z)-\frac{1}{\lambda}\sum_{i=1}^{N}p_{i}q_{i}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A7.p24" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.p24.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.p24.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Conclusion:
<br class="ltx_break"><span id="A7.p24.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium">The gradient is exactly the Shannon entropy of the probability distribution <math id="A7.p24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math> :</span></span></p>
</div>
<div id="A7.p25" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A7.Ex61" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.Ex61.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\frac{\partial f}{\partial\lambda}=H(p)=-\sum_{i=1}^{N}p_{i}\log\left(p_{i}\right)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mi>H</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.055em">−</mo><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mi>log</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\partial f}{\partial\lambda}=H(p)=-\sum_{i=1}^{N}p_{i}\log\left(p_{i}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A7.p25.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.p25.1.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A7.p26" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.p26.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.p26.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Interpretation of the whole gradient</span>
Therefore, we can interpret the gradient of (<a href="#A7.E30" title="Equation 30 ‣ Appendix G Automatic temperature tuning ‣ SiMPO: Measure Matching for Online Diffusion Reinforcement Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">30</span></a>) as</p>
<table id="A7.Ex62" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A7.Ex62.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon+H(p)-\log N" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon+H(p)-\log N</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A7.p26.2" class="ltx_p">where</p>
<ul id="A7.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A7.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A7.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A7.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log N</annotation></semantics></math> is the entropy of a uniform distribution, which is the <span id="A7.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">maximum possible entropy</span> of a discrete distribution on <math id="A7.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> variables. FOr our case, as we select <math id="A7.I1.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N=32" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>32</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N=32</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="A7.I1.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log N\approx 3.47" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo>≈</mo><mn>3.47</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log N\approx 3.47</annotation></semantics></math>;</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A7.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A7.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A7.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H(p)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H(p)</annotation></semantics></math> is the entropy of current reweighting distribution, <math id="A7.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{softmax}(q_{i}/\lambda)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>softmax</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{softmax}(q_{i}/\lambda)</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A7.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A7.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A7.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math> controls the gap between the current entropy and a fully uniform distribution.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</section>
